.TH CVEC_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvec_construct \- type-inferred vector construction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvec_construct(vec_name, type);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This type-inferred macro creates a vector, finding the element size from
the type automatically. It also makes a type marker variable, which tells
the other type-dispatching macros the declared element type at each call
site.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
vec_name  Name of the vector variable to create
type      Element type, for example int, double or struct foo
          Any type name is accepted, including a function
          pointer type such as void (*)(int) and an array
          type such as int[4]. For an array element type,
          give cvec_push(3) an array or a string literal.
          The macro copies its bytes into the element
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro stops the program when an allocation fails.
The macro makes a hidden type marker variable that the other
type-dispatching macros read; cvec_redeclare(3) makes it again in another
scope.
The macro is equal to cvector_create(sizeof(type), &err) with error
handling.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cvec_construct(my_vec, int);
cvec_push(my_vec, 42);
cvec_destroy(my_vec);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_construct_scoped (3),
.BR cvector_create (3)
